[-] Pilot coordination with existing tools and measure reliance =coordination-pilot $Executed 2026-09-14, two runs (report knowledge/evaluations/coordination-pilot-report.md, commits a6454b9 + a46ebad). Run 1: changed-support PASSED, honest-impossibility PASSED, scope-expansion declined, reuse-without-rereading FAILED (reconstruction cheaper at 50-line scale), wrong-but-current claim undetected, both §1 trust limits reproduced, CC1 live. Run 2 (load-bearing probe): reliance arm DETECTED the planted false claim and superseded it, but declined to break the documented design rule against a direct instruction (both readings recorded); control arm implemented the fix overriding the rule. Sharpest gap unchanged: repo-wide orientation vs worktree truth -> workstreams-sessions; all else maps to none. Pending: coordination-selection disposition; platform submodule addendum optional.$ !2 ^2026-09-14T14:28 <contextual-freshness <collective-agency-protocol #01a0a1d2-318f-76a3-b3d7-4bb8ef380c63
[ ] Specify external intent changes and completion write-back failures =coordination-authority-boundary $Read knowledge/decisions/external-workspace-and-clearhead-boundary.md first. Design only unsettled semantics: bound action revised, cancelled or unavailable; explicit completion write-back partly fails. Define source reference/version, reorientation points, unavailable versus unchanged, retry/recovery and lifecycle authority. Acceptance: executable scenario definitions distinguish ready, Git-landed, validated and externally completed; no automatic Clearhead completion, history rewriting, permission grants or mandatory Clearhead dependency. Precedes selected structured handoff implementation; no general synchronization.$ !2 ^2026-09-14T14:28 <coordination-selection #01a0a1d2-31a8-78e1-8d49-eb2c97c65807
[ ] Scope shared orientation to the querying worktree =orientation-worktree-context $Selected by coordination-selection (knowledge/decisions/coordination-selection-disposition.md, 2026-09-14) as the ONLY work item justified by the pilot. Owner directive: no explicit coordination machinery in code or guidance; the substrate IS the shared intentions board, linked not built-in. Scope: (1) serve the worktree context field in CLI/MCP status and delta JSON (projection structs define it today; the CLI drops it) so cross-harness consumers can see which context verdicts were computed for; (2) scope session-orientation summaries (e.g. Claude SessionStart) to the querying worktree so landed state from another branch never reads as true locally (pilot run 1, control-arm finding). No workstream/session/declaration/handoff entities; foreign-repo agents rely on claims+Git and links, never a required CLI. Acceptance: status/delta carry worktree context; a summary opened in a worktree on branch X does not present branch Y commits as landed; cross-harness spot check in plot.$ !3 +implementation ^2026-09-14T18:22 #01a0a2a8-42cb-72d0-8af5-ed80b305bcca
